1
00:00:42,539 --> 00:00:43,457
What the heck?!

2
00:00:43,482 --> 00:00:44,523
I’m sorry.

3
00:00:47,359 --> 00:00:48,359
Who was that?

4
00:00:50,613 --> 00:00:52,740
Nobody will admit it?

5
00:00:55,534 --> 00:00:58,079
Mr. Araneta and Mr. Morato!

6
00:00:58,579 --> 00:01:00,000
You two again?!

7
00:01:04,089 --> 00:01:04,965
Sir, sorry, sir.

8
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:06,116
It won’t happen again.

9
00:01:06,309 --> 00:01:07,435
Definitely not!

10
00:01:07,922 --> 00:01:09,506
Now, answer this problem

11
00:01:09,507 --> 00:01:11,217
if you don't want to get hit!

12
00:01:12,301 --> 00:01:13,302
Listen.

13
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:19,024
Mr. Morato gets hit by my ruler three times

14
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:21,685
out of five recitations.

15
00:01:22,228 --> 00:01:28,234
And Mr. Araneta gets hit
by my ruler two out of five.

16
00:01:28,508 --> 00:01:31,011
Now, if I call on both of you,

17
00:01:31,487 --> 00:01:33,780
what is the exact percentage

18
00:01:33,781 --> 00:01:35,825
that you won't get hit by this ruler?

19
00:01:40,037 --> 00:01:41,037
Three...

20
00:01:41,956 --> 00:01:42,748
Two...

21
00:01:42,957 --> 00:01:44,291
Thirty three...

22
00:01:44,708 --> 00:01:46,418
Sir, what kind of question is that?

23
00:01:47,962 --> 00:01:48,962
Five...

24
00:01:49,547 --> 00:01:50,547
Four...

25
00:01:52,216 --> 00:01:53,425
Three...

26
00:01:54,176 --> 00:01:55,094
- Fifty! Fifty!
- Two...

27
00:01:55,094 --> 00:01:56,053
- Fifty percent!
- Fifty.

28
00:01:56,053 --> 00:01:56,804
That’s right!

29
00:01:56,805 --> 00:01:57,805
Fifty?

30
00:01:59,932 --> 00:02:01,016
Impressive!

31
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,633
Impressive! Class!

32
00:02:03,936 --> 00:02:05,646
Give them a round of applause!

33
00:02:10,317 --> 00:02:13,194
Because of that, you get a reward.

34
00:02:13,195 --> 00:02:14,822
Get here in front.

35
00:02:15,114 --> 00:02:16,197
Come on, come on.

36
00:02:16,198 --> 00:02:17,241
Come to the front.

37
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,374
Because you are so sure

38
00:02:26,375 --> 00:02:27,877
that the answer is fifty...

39
00:02:28,044 --> 00:02:28,836
That’s correct.

40
00:02:28,861 --> 00:02:30,945
You're getting fifty hits with the ruler.

41
00:02:32,047 --> 00:02:33,174
My goodness.

42
00:02:33,502 --> 00:02:34,485
Fifty?!

43
00:02:34,611 --> 00:02:35,237
Huh?

44
00:02:35,262 --> 00:02:36,179
Oh, sir, it was only one percent.

45
00:02:36,179 --> 00:02:36,930
So, just one hit!

46
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:37,347
One percent?!

47
00:02:37,348 --> 00:02:38,557
Just one hit!

48
00:02:39,016 --> 00:02:39,558
Sir...

49
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,642
Just one percent. Right.

50
00:02:42,119 --> 00:02:43,871
Who can solve the problem? Who?

51
00:02:44,051 --> 00:02:45,135
Come on.

52
00:02:46,051 --> 00:02:46,790
Oh!

53
00:02:46,955 --> 00:02:48,749
Yes, Mr. Chua?

54
00:02:51,851 --> 00:02:53,519
Twenty four percent, sir.

55
00:02:53,908 --> 00:02:54,909
Correct!

56
00:02:55,034 --> 00:02:56,160
Very good!

57
00:02:56,285 --> 00:02:57,493
Such a show-off, huh?

58
00:02:57,494 --> 00:02:58,704
- So full of himself.
- Show off.

59
00:02:58,829 --> 00:03:01,029
- Give him a round of applause!
- Who does he think he is?

60
00:03:01,624 --> 00:03:03,334
Look at him, acting all...

61
00:03:07,050 --> 00:03:08,135
You know the drill.

62
00:03:09,592 --> 00:03:10,967
Please don’t do this, sir.

63
00:03:10,992 --> 00:03:13,161
- Sir, please.
- Sir, just one.

64
00:03:13,302 --> 00:03:15,011
Alright!

65
00:03:15,012 --> 00:03:17,723
Hands on the table!
Come on, come on!

66
00:03:18,432 --> 00:03:20,059
You're such troublemakers!

67
00:03:20,749 --> 00:03:21,791
Sir, please don’t do this.

68
00:03:21,816 --> 00:03:23,651
Sir, we won’t do it again.

69
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:26,607
Ouch! Sir!

70
00:03:27,024 --> 00:03:27,566
Ouch!

71
00:03:27,566 --> 00:03:28,566
Sir!

72
00:03:36,909 --> 00:03:37,909
Ma’am!

73
00:03:37,998 --> 00:03:40,249
It's already 2016,
and you're still hitting students!

74
00:03:40,274 --> 00:03:41,586
That's not allowed anymore!

75
00:03:42,957 --> 00:03:45,292
Ma’am, give Aira her microphone back.

76
00:03:45,459 --> 00:03:47,085
She just wants to be a news presenter,

77
00:03:47,086 --> 00:03:48,686
that's why she always carries it around.

78
00:03:50,214 --> 00:03:51,589
Give me your headband!

79
00:03:51,590 --> 00:03:52,258
Ma’am!

80
00:03:52,259 --> 00:03:53,968
I just bought that!

81
00:03:55,010 --> 00:03:57,721
Ma’am, I promise.
When I become a news anchor,

82
00:03:57,888 --> 00:04:00,307
I'll make you the star of my own TV show.

83
00:04:01,642 --> 00:04:02,810
Dear...

84
00:04:03,352 --> 00:04:05,771
You need to graduate first.

85
00:04:05,938 --> 00:04:08,524
Before you can achieve that dream of yours.

86
00:04:08,970 --> 00:04:11,067
But ma’am, Aira's a smart girl.

87
00:04:11,068 --> 00:04:13,487
Wasn't she 29th in the exam?

88
00:04:13,862 --> 00:04:15,656
Out of 37?

89
00:04:18,784 --> 00:04:21,245
What about you, Miss 35th Place?

90
00:04:21,912 --> 00:04:23,706
Do you want to be a news anchor too?

91
00:04:24,206 --> 00:04:25,165
No, ma'am.

92
00:04:25,166 --> 00:04:26,709
I just want to be a housewife.

93
00:04:30,296 --> 00:04:31,296
Alright, then!

94
00:04:31,588 --> 00:04:34,049
You'll get your confiscated things back

95
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:36,468
once you've cleaned the auditorium.

96
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:38,971
Ma’am, can we do it tomorrow instead?

97
00:04:39,555 --> 00:04:41,181
Then you'll get them tomorrow.

98
00:04:41,390 --> 00:04:42,390
Huh?

99
00:04:43,142 --> 00:04:44,977
- Ma’am!
- Ma’am!

100
00:04:45,394 --> 00:04:47,062
My headband.

101
00:04:55,612 --> 00:04:56,612
It looks pretty.

102
00:04:58,741 --> 00:04:59,741
Girl!

103
00:05:00,242 --> 00:05:00,993
Yeah?

104
00:05:01,118 --> 00:05:04,246
The milky polvoron is sold out again!

105
00:05:04,455 --> 00:05:05,581
Seriously?!

106
00:05:05,748 --> 00:05:07,249
Where am I supposed to buy that now?

107
00:05:07,416 --> 00:05:09,543
Do you know where I can buy some?

108
00:05:11,879 --> 00:05:13,756
Susie, here’s your favorite.

109
00:05:13,922 --> 00:05:15,674
I already bought you some earlier.

110
00:05:15,966 --> 00:05:18,509
Don't buy me stuff like this, Marvin.

111
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:20,721
Your mom might scold me again.

112
00:05:22,014 --> 00:05:23,974
Are you going to tutoring later?

113
00:05:24,683 --> 00:05:25,683
No.

114
00:05:25,893 --> 00:05:26,977
I’ll skip class today.

115
00:05:27,227 --> 00:05:28,854
I have somewhere to be in Ortigas.

116
00:05:29,521 --> 00:05:30,647
In Ortigas?

117
00:05:30,898 --> 00:05:31,898
Why?

118
00:05:32,941 --> 00:05:34,318
None of your business.

119
00:05:37,529 --> 00:05:38,739
Hiyah!

120
00:05:48,332 --> 00:05:50,167
He didn't notice me.

121
00:06:05,015 --> 00:06:06,182
Why does it taste like this?

122
00:06:06,183 --> 00:06:06,809
What’s wrong?

123
00:06:06,999 --> 00:06:07,791
It tastes like...

124
00:06:07,816 --> 00:06:08,816
Spring rolls?

125
00:06:10,145 --> 00:06:10,729
Wow.

126
00:06:10,730 --> 00:06:14,982
It tastes like peanuts fried
in the vendor’s used cooking oil.

127
00:06:14,983 --> 00:06:17,444
So you're a chef now, huh?
I wasn’t informed.

128
00:06:18,844 --> 00:06:19,844
It tastes like...

129
00:06:21,492 --> 00:06:23,452
What kind of outfit is that?

130
00:06:25,202 --> 00:06:26,245
Why? Look.

131
00:06:27,913 --> 00:06:29,123
So they match!

132
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,600
Is that what you're wearing underneath?

133
00:06:32,167 --> 00:06:33,377
Does Susie know about that?

134
00:06:34,253 --> 00:06:35,253
Susie?

135
00:06:35,671 --> 00:06:37,047
Why? Does she need to know?

136
00:06:37,338 --> 00:06:38,338
Of course.

137
00:06:38,549 --> 00:06:39,882
You're the school's best fighter.

138
00:06:39,883 --> 00:06:41,802
And she's the leader of the girls.

139
00:06:42,177 --> 00:06:42,886
That's it!

140
00:06:42,887 --> 00:06:44,138
You two are a perfect match.

141
00:06:44,296 --> 00:06:45,338
That's what suits you.

142
00:06:45,806 --> 00:06:46,806
Perfect match?

143
00:06:47,391 --> 00:06:48,391
Why?

144
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:51,353
Does Susie like me?

145
00:06:56,191 --> 00:06:58,569
You're given milky polvoron every day.

146
00:06:59,350 --> 00:07:00,392
What do you think?

147
00:07:02,823 --> 00:07:05,784
Have a nice day - Susie.

148
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:08,035
If you ask me,
if I ever have a girlfriend,

149
00:07:08,036 --> 00:07:09,396
I really don't want someone tacky.

150
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:12,624
You're so harsh.

151
00:07:13,876 --> 00:07:14,876
Look at me.

152
00:07:15,377 --> 00:07:16,503
I look cool.

153
00:07:37,232 --> 00:07:38,232
Melvin...

154
00:07:38,738 --> 00:07:39,489
Melvin, right?

155
00:07:39,514 --> 00:07:40,194
Melvin?

156
00:07:40,195 --> 00:07:41,444
No. Marvin.

157
00:07:41,445 --> 00:07:42,863
Marvin! Yeah, Marvin!

158
00:07:43,112 --> 00:07:45,990
Marvin, maybe you
could sponsor my friend here.

159
00:07:46,450 --> 00:07:48,160
Maybe you could lend him your shirt.

160
00:07:48,185 --> 00:07:49,227
Yes, please.

161
00:07:50,746 --> 00:07:52,374
He's going to Ortigas later.

162
00:07:52,399 --> 00:07:53,900
For the National Sports Festival.

163
00:07:54,458 --> 00:07:55,458
Don’t worry.

164
00:07:55,709 --> 00:07:57,044
He’ll give it back to you.

165
00:07:59,129 --> 00:08:00,255
In Ortigas?

166
00:08:00,422 --> 00:08:01,422
Yes, in Ortigas.

167
00:08:01,673 --> 00:08:03,217
He has a Taekwondo match.

168
00:08:03,509 --> 00:08:04,384
If he wins,

169
00:08:04,409 --> 00:08:05,719
of course, if he takes it off like this,

170
00:08:05,844 --> 00:08:07,513
his shirt is branded.

171
00:08:07,804 --> 00:08:08,930
And then the crowd will start cheering.

172
00:08:08,931 --> 00:08:10,451
Then they will think he is a city boy.

173
00:08:11,266 --> 00:08:12,267
Let's trade!

174
00:08:12,976 --> 00:08:14,602
This is always sold out at the canteen.

175
00:08:14,603 --> 00:08:15,218
Yes.

176
00:08:15,521 --> 00:08:17,063
Right?

177
00:08:17,064 --> 00:08:17,814
This tastes good.

178
00:08:17,814 --> 00:08:18,814
It’s delicious.

179
00:08:18,857 --> 00:08:20,526
Yeah, this polvoron is delicious.

180
00:08:21,568 --> 00:08:22,903
Please, please?

181
00:08:23,904 --> 00:08:25,072
Marvin, come on.

182
00:08:38,168 --> 00:08:39,670
What time is his match?

183
00:08:39,962 --> 00:08:42,088
Hmm, 6 P.M.?

184
00:08:42,089 --> 00:08:44,675
We need to leave by 3 P.M.

185
00:08:45,509 --> 00:08:47,553
I hope there’s no traffic on NLEX.

186
00:08:47,970 --> 00:08:48,970
Right.

187
00:08:50,943 --> 00:08:51,943
Let me see.

188
00:08:53,725 --> 00:08:54,726
Let’s practice.

189
00:09:00,857 --> 00:09:02,066
Ma’am...

190
00:09:02,067 --> 00:09:04,652
Ma’am, I think we’re
coming down with a fever.

191
00:09:04,653 --> 00:09:06,363
Maybe...

192
00:09:06,655 --> 00:09:08,755
Maybe we could go home now?

193
00:09:10,110 --> 00:09:11,677
You’re right.

194
00:09:11,702 --> 00:09:14,997
Your lips are looking pale.

195
00:09:17,295 --> 00:09:18,295
Now what?

196
00:09:18,371 --> 00:09:19,372
What’s that?

197
00:09:20,816 --> 00:09:21,731
We’re sorry.

198
00:09:23,637 --> 00:09:24,972
- We’re busted.
- Seriously!

199
00:09:27,050 --> 00:09:28,218
These kids!

200
00:09:28,635 --> 00:09:30,596
Ouch! Ahh!

201
00:09:32,598 --> 00:09:33,598
Ma’am!

202
00:09:33,765 --> 00:09:34,932
It hurts!

203
00:09:34,933 --> 00:09:37,518
I got hit by a sepak takraw ball
during PE class.

204
00:09:37,519 --> 00:09:39,354
My back hurts so much.

205
00:09:39,479 --> 00:09:40,647
Her bones are broken.

206
00:09:40,772 --> 00:09:43,275
Ahh! Don't touch it! It hurts!

207
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:45,319
It really hurts. It hurts so much!

208
00:09:46,570 --> 00:09:47,195
Ouch!

209
00:09:47,279 --> 00:09:49,114
- It hurts, doesn't it?
- Slowly.

210
00:09:49,323 --> 00:09:51,700
Then why is your face
the one that's bruised, huh?

211
00:09:58,286 --> 00:09:59,454
You're unbelievable!

212
00:10:04,834 --> 00:10:06,503
You're really out of it, Aira!

213
00:10:07,684 --> 00:10:10,353
You know, we actually could leave
without your mic.

214
00:10:10,886 --> 00:10:11,887
No way!

215
00:10:12,137 --> 00:10:13,137
I need that.

216
00:10:19,770 --> 00:10:21,605
Should we just say we broke our leg?

217
00:10:25,567 --> 00:10:26,567
Like this?

218
00:10:27,152 --> 00:10:27,986
Or this?

219
00:10:27,987 --> 00:10:29,695
Oh, forget it!

220
00:10:29,696 --> 00:10:30,696
It’s too much.

221
00:10:30,739 --> 00:10:31,739
It’s unbelievable.

222
00:10:35,369 --> 00:10:36,870
Who on earth...

223
00:10:38,413 --> 00:10:40,832
Who touched my car again?

224
00:10:41,083 --> 00:10:42,501
That is brand new!

225
00:10:46,505 --> 00:10:47,881
I have an idea.

226
00:10:48,256 --> 00:10:49,466
Come on, hurry!

227
00:11:06,441 --> 00:11:07,025
Ms. Conti!

228
00:11:07,442 --> 00:11:08,568
Ms. Padilla!

229
00:11:09,778 --> 00:11:11,029
Hey!

230
00:11:11,279 --> 00:11:12,823
You guys are such a pain!

231
00:11:12,989 --> 00:11:13,824
W.O.L.O.!

232
00:11:13,825 --> 00:11:15,492
We Only Live Once!

233
00:11:15,742 --> 00:11:16,410
How about tomorrow?

234
00:11:16,410 --> 00:11:17,077
Let’s see!

235
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,160
Screw it!

236
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:26,460
Kick!

237
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:29,630
Kick!

238
00:11:29,965 --> 00:11:31,299
Kick him!

239
00:11:34,094 --> 00:11:35,594
Let's cheer even louder!

240
00:11:35,595 --> 00:11:37,221
Don’t get intimidated by
those guys from Manila.

241
00:11:37,222 --> 00:11:39,141
We know Hanz way better
than they do, right?

242
00:11:42,686 --> 00:11:44,855
Go, go, go!

243
00:11:45,105 --> 00:11:47,399
Kick him!

244
00:11:47,816 --> 00:11:49,735
Here comes mic girl again.

245
00:11:53,447 --> 00:11:55,990
The cheer! We need a cheer!
One, two, three, go!

246
00:11:55,991 --> 00:11:59,493
Go, go, go, go, Hanz!

247
00:11:59,494 --> 00:12:01,245
Go, go, go, go, Hanz!

248
00:12:01,246 --> 00:12:04,666
Hanz-some!

249
00:12:08,003 --> 00:12:11,965
You're the Bruce Lee of Bulacan!

250
00:12:18,305 --> 00:12:19,597
That’s so loud.

251
00:12:19,598 --> 00:12:21,223
My ears are hurting.

252
00:12:21,224 --> 00:12:22,934
Well, they’re from the province.

253
00:12:23,393 --> 00:12:26,646
Their houses are far apart
so they're used to shouting.

254
00:12:29,274 --> 00:12:31,526
Hanz, get up! Get up!

255
00:12:37,574 --> 00:12:38,867
Fight!

256
00:12:39,493 --> 00:12:42,578
Go, go, go, go, Hanz!

257
00:12:42,579 --> 00:12:46,874
Go, go, go, go, Hanz!
Hanz-some!

258
00:12:46,875 --> 00:12:48,168
She’s really loud.

259
00:12:49,503 --> 00:12:50,920
Excuse me.

260
00:12:50,921 --> 00:12:53,799
Excuse me.
Miss, give way, thank you.

261
00:12:54,466 --> 00:12:55,634
Susie!

262
00:12:56,343 --> 00:12:58,887
Hey, what are you doing here?

263
00:12:59,513 --> 00:13:02,766
Why did you give Hanz
the milky polvoron that I gave you?

264
00:13:03,433 --> 00:13:06,018
You seriously came here
just to ask me that?

265
00:13:06,019 --> 00:13:07,853
Don’t you have a class?

266
00:13:07,854 --> 00:13:09,356
Do you like Hanz?

267
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:48,353
Two, one!

268
00:14:21,970 --> 00:14:24,847
From now on, I'm your boyfriend!

269
00:14:24,848 --> 00:14:26,600
Let's go out on a date!

270
00:14:28,435 --> 00:14:29,644
Susie!

271
00:14:32,689 --> 00:14:35,566
He says it's me!

272
00:14:35,567 --> 00:14:38,944
Susie, you are the milk to my coffee.

273
00:14:38,945 --> 00:14:41,907
And I'm the dried fish
to your chocolate porridge.

274
00:14:42,490 --> 00:14:44,408
We’re the perfect match, Susie.

275
00:14:44,409 --> 00:14:48,038
1-4-3-7-7-9-6-6-6-6!

276
00:14:51,166 --> 00:14:52,792
I love you, Susie!

277
00:14:59,758 --> 00:15:00,675
Ouch! Coach!

278
00:15:00,676 --> 00:15:03,010
Why did you give away your uniform?

279
00:15:03,011 --> 00:15:04,888
You’re unbelievable!

280
00:15:09,309 --> 00:15:11,435
<i>He was only sent to Manila to train,</i>

281
00:15:11,436 --> 00:15:13,355
<i>and now he's doing ridiculous things.</i>

282
00:15:17,192 --> 00:15:19,194
Are you really going on a date with him?

283
00:15:19,444 --> 00:15:20,444
Of course!

284
00:15:20,445 --> 00:15:22,530
He doesn't even know
how to compute probability!

285
00:15:22,906 --> 00:15:25,533
And he always get
hit with a ruler in class.

286
00:15:25,951 --> 00:15:27,785
And he doesn’t know how to dress up.

287
00:15:27,786 --> 00:15:30,162
Well to me, he's still cool.

288
00:15:30,163 --> 00:15:32,415
Because he's the best player at our school.

289
00:15:32,624 --> 00:15:35,126
And you know me,
I only date the best.

290
00:15:47,973 --> 00:15:49,181
- Excuse me.
- Ouch!

291
00:15:49,182 --> 00:15:49,891
Excuse!

292
00:15:49,891 --> 00:15:50,725
What’s wrong with you?!

293
00:15:50,725 --> 00:15:51,725
Excuse me!

294
00:15:53,728 --> 00:15:55,939
Friend, sorry, she didn't mean to.

295
00:15:56,398 --> 00:15:57,691
You’re so annoying!

296
00:16:02,821 --> 00:16:04,061
I already said sorry, didn't I?

297
00:16:06,658 --> 00:16:09,035
<i>If we used to be called the Fantastic Four,</i>

298
00:16:09,869 --> 00:16:11,538
<i>are we still fantastic now?</i>

299
00:16:16,876 --> 00:16:19,546
<i>The former mic girl who wants
to become a news anchor.</i>

300
00:16:20,005 --> 00:16:22,424
Excuse me.

301
00:16:22,757 --> 00:16:23,799
Sorry.

302
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:26,219
Excuse me.

303
00:16:26,594 --> 00:16:27,929
Make way please.

304
00:16:28,596 --> 00:16:29,097
Thank you.

305
00:16:29,097 --> 00:16:29,681
Good morning, ma’am.

306
00:16:29,681 --> 00:16:30,681
Good morning.

307
00:16:31,474 --> 00:16:33,518
Who is she anyway?
Is that a VIP?

308
00:16:35,145 --> 00:16:36,062
Good morning.

309
00:16:36,062 --> 00:16:37,062
Good morning, ma’am.

310
00:16:51,411 --> 00:16:54,956
<i>She ended up at a mall information
desk as a concierge.</i>

311
00:16:55,290 --> 00:16:57,499
Good morning!
Welcome to Mega Lux mall!

312
00:16:57,500 --> 00:17:00,462
Enjoy your shopping!
Keep smiling!

313
00:17:04,549 --> 00:17:05,925
Good morning!

314
00:17:06,051 --> 00:17:11,681
<i>The taekwondo prodigy who wants to show off
his signature roundhouse kick.</i>

315
00:17:13,016 --> 00:17:14,142
Good morning, sir.

316
00:17:25,487 --> 00:17:27,489
<i>He is now kicking pests instead.</i>

317
00:17:29,324 --> 00:17:31,951
<i>The pink princess who wants
to become a housewife.</i>

318
00:17:42,378 --> 00:17:46,549
<i>She is now handling customers
as a customer service agent.</i>

319
00:17:48,468 --> 00:17:50,677
Hello? This is Shop Shop Baby.

320
00:17:50,678 --> 00:17:52,930
Your One-Stop Home TV Shop.

321
00:17:52,931 --> 00:17:54,307
How may I help you?

322
00:17:55,308 --> 00:17:58,978
<i>The convenient store enthusiast
with a unique taste palate.</i>

323
00:18:07,695 --> 00:18:08,988
Good morning, sir.

324
00:18:21,417 --> 00:18:24,838
<i>He became a merchandise buyer
for a home shopping channel.</i>

325
00:18:25,463 --> 00:18:27,006
This is really crispy.

326
00:18:27,590 --> 00:18:30,301
Miss, is there a discount
if I order 2,000 packs?

327
00:18:32,178 --> 00:18:33,471
<i>This is who we are now.</i>

328
00:18:34,055 --> 00:18:36,181
<i>None of our dreams came true.</i>

329
00:18:36,182 --> 00:18:39,060
<i>But we continue to fight
through life's hardships.</i>

330
00:18:39,561 --> 00:18:40,937
<i>This is our story.</i>

331
00:18:41,437 --> 00:18:43,857
<i>We are all fighting for our way.</i>

332
00:18:50,488 --> 00:18:51,865
[How was your exam?]

333
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,616
<i>Why aren't you answering?</i>

334
00:18:54,534 --> 00:18:55,869
<i>Did you fail again?</i>

335
00:18:58,845 --> 00:19:02,515
Welcome!
Enjoy shopping! Keep smiling!

336
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:04,561
Aira?

337
00:19:04,586 --> 00:19:05,420
Keep smili...

338
00:19:05,474 --> 00:19:07,309
Aira, it’s you!

339
00:19:09,591 --> 00:19:11,634
So, you work here now?

340
00:19:11,899 --> 00:19:13,192
Wow!

341
00:19:13,636 --> 00:19:15,054
Good for you!

342
00:19:15,555 --> 00:19:18,433
Anyway, let's have a reunion soon.

343
00:19:18,892 --> 00:19:19,892
Wait!

344
00:19:19,976 --> 00:19:21,477
Let me give you my card.

345
00:19:26,524 --> 00:19:28,109
Here, so you can contact me.

346
00:19:32,238 --> 00:19:33,822
Alright, I’ll get going.

347
00:19:33,823 --> 00:19:35,742
I still have a client meeting to catch.

348
00:19:35,867 --> 00:19:38,745
Otherwise, we could’ve spent
more time catching up.

349
00:19:40,872 --> 00:19:41,956
Nice seeing you again.

350
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:44,000
Bye!

351
00:19:55,136 --> 00:19:57,055
When I was in Grade 5,

352
00:19:57,472 --> 00:19:59,265
David Licauco was my classmate.

353
00:20:00,058 --> 00:20:01,601
The famous actor.

354
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:03,068
That handsome guy.

355
00:20:05,855 --> 00:20:07,190
Is my voice too loud?

356
00:20:10,265 --> 00:20:11,265
Oh, sorry.

357
00:20:12,702 --> 00:20:14,079
But I’m telling you,

358
00:20:14,656 --> 00:20:15,949
he was always sleeping.

359
00:20:16,574 --> 00:20:18,201
I’m way better-looking than him.

360
00:20:32,548 --> 00:20:33,591
Not here.

361
00:20:34,759 --> 00:20:35,759
Huh?

362
00:20:38,096 --> 00:20:39,096
Oh...

363
00:20:39,138 --> 00:20:40,138
Sorry.

364
00:20:42,350 --> 00:20:43,767
Just to change the subject.

365
00:20:43,768 --> 00:20:46,145
Phil mentioned that you're a specialist?

366
00:20:46,562 --> 00:20:47,605
Are you a doctor?

367
00:20:48,231 --> 00:20:49,399
Something like that.

368
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:54,460
I help keep the clients
from getting scabies.

369
00:20:54,988 --> 00:20:56,948
Oh! Are you a dermatologist?

370
00:20:58,032 --> 00:21:00,660
Well, skincare is important these days.

371
00:21:05,456 --> 00:21:11,129
<i>Dr. Pest Alis, drives the pests away!</i>

372
00:21:13,631 --> 00:21:16,467
Oh, by the way,
I brought our company car.

373
00:21:16,759 --> 00:21:17,969
So? Can I take you home?

374
00:21:18,766 --> 00:21:20,601
No, thanks. I’m fine.

375
00:21:21,014 --> 00:21:22,014
Are you sure?

376
00:21:22,039 --> 00:21:24,599
Fares are so expensive these days.

377
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:25,476
It would be such a waste.

378
00:21:25,477 --> 00:21:27,854
You can use that to pay for your apartment.

379
00:21:28,313 --> 00:21:30,189
I’m on an annual lease anyway.

380
00:21:31,106 --> 00:21:31,815
What?

381
00:21:32,154 --> 00:21:33,197
Annual lease?

382
00:21:34,068 --> 00:21:35,569
You must be rich.

383
00:21:35,570 --> 00:21:36,810
I didn't know you’re that rich.

384
00:21:37,731 --> 00:21:41,026
Anyway, I heard you used to be popular at…

385
00:21:41,387 --> 00:21:42,805
What sport was that again?

386
00:21:50,418 --> 00:21:51,827
I didn't play any sports.

387
00:21:52,729 --> 00:21:53,730
Oh, okay.

388
00:22:03,348 --> 00:22:05,074
Sorry for the inconvenience.

389
00:22:05,099 --> 00:22:08,936
Did I get it right?
The blanket you got smells like fart?

390
00:22:09,621 --> 00:22:11,381
<i>It’s like someone
deliberately farted on it.</i>

391
00:22:11,606 --> 00:22:13,646
<i>Why don’t you come over here
and smell it yourself!</i>

392
00:22:13,671 --> 00:22:14,671
Oh...

393
00:22:15,193 --> 00:22:16,527
I have rhinitis, sir.

394
00:22:16,611 --> 00:22:18,821
I can't even smell my own fart.

395
00:22:20,990 --> 00:22:23,868
But since you're sensitive,

396
00:22:24,494 --> 00:22:27,038
I'll just help you process a refund.

397
00:22:27,205 --> 00:22:27,747
Uh...

398
00:22:27,872 --> 00:22:30,208
Are you Bona Delgado?

399
00:22:30,708 --> 00:22:32,585
<i>No. I’m her husband.</i>

400
00:22:32,983 --> 00:22:34,150
Oh, okay.

401
00:22:34,980 --> 00:22:36,898
Then, why are you the one calling?

402
00:22:36,923 --> 00:22:37,923
<i>What did you say?</i>

403
00:22:38,174 --> 00:22:39,175
<i>I can’t hear you!</i>

404
00:22:40,343 --> 00:22:41,928
Your nose really is sensitive, sir.

405
00:22:41,953 --> 00:22:43,413
At least your ears make up for it.

406
00:22:43,763 --> 00:22:45,556
<i>Do your job properly!</i>

407
00:22:45,723 --> 00:22:47,392
I paid so much for this!

408
00:22:50,436 --> 00:22:51,520
Hello, sir?

409
00:22:51,521 --> 00:22:52,105
<i>Who is this?!</i>

410
00:22:52,106 --> 00:22:53,106
Good morning, sir.

411
00:22:53,107 --> 00:22:55,787
<i>- My morning couldn't get any worse!</i>
- So sorry for the inconvenience.

412
00:22:56,275 --> 00:22:58,236
Sir, how can I help you, sir?

413
00:22:58,361 --> 00:22:59,779
<i>Your product is terrible!</i>

414
00:22:59,904 --> 00:23:00,530
Oh, okay.

415
00:23:00,530 --> 00:23:01,530
<i>I want a refund!</i>

416
00:23:02,031 --> 00:23:03,324
Alright.

417
00:23:04,450 --> 00:23:06,452
I don’t know what to do with you anymore.

418
00:23:06,869 --> 00:23:07,869
I’m so frustrated!

419
00:23:07,870 --> 00:23:09,204
I’ve told you this so many times already!

420
00:23:09,205 --> 00:23:11,124
I’ve already given you
two chances to train.

421
00:23:11,791 --> 00:23:13,500
Do you understand?
Make sure you get it right!

422
00:23:13,501 --> 00:23:16,962
I’m so frustrated!
I keep repeating myself.

423
00:23:16,963 --> 00:23:18,005
Faster!

424
00:23:22,969 --> 00:23:24,345
Marie, right?

425
00:23:24,762 --> 00:23:25,762
You’re Marie?

426
00:23:25,972 --> 00:23:26,972
Yes, sir.

427
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:28,420
Is this for the conference room?

428
00:23:28,850 --> 00:23:30,601
Oh, yes. I'm almost done.

429
00:23:31,185 --> 00:23:32,937
Alright, I’ll just do it myself.

430
00:23:33,396 --> 00:23:34,814
Are you sure?

431
00:23:35,606 --> 00:23:37,483
I need 100 sheets.

432
00:23:38,484 --> 00:23:40,236
It’s okay.
I like doing this.

433
00:23:49,968 --> 00:23:52,706
They already look down on our work.

434
00:23:52,988 --> 00:23:56,324
And idiots like you are
only making it worse.

435
00:23:56,377 --> 00:23:57,670
Do you have a boyfriend?

436
00:23:59,547 --> 00:24:00,715
Yes, I have one.

437
00:24:01,257 --> 00:24:02,507
What’s the relevance?

438
00:24:02,508 --> 00:24:04,469
Then why don't you just get married?

439
00:24:07,847 --> 00:24:08,847
Oh...

440
00:24:09,849 --> 00:24:10,892
We have a meeting here.

441
00:24:11,100 --> 00:24:13,853
Oh, sorry, sir.
We’re also done here.

442
00:24:14,145 --> 00:24:15,813
Get your work done properly.

443
00:24:35,124 --> 00:24:36,334
I need a minute.

444
00:24:36,417 --> 00:24:37,418
The might see us.

445
00:24:37,460 --> 00:24:39,045
I need to recharge.

446
00:24:44,050 --> 00:24:45,968
You went here because of me, didn’t you?

447
00:24:46,594 --> 00:24:48,234
Your meeting isn't for another two hours.

448
00:24:51,182 --> 00:24:52,308
You...

449
00:24:53,434 --> 00:24:55,561
What did you do this time, hon?

450
00:24:57,563 --> 00:24:59,857
Hon, I think I need to get married.

451
00:25:02,068 --> 00:25:03,068
Huh?

452
00:25:05,154 --> 00:25:07,073
What are you saying this time?

453
00:25:08,032 --> 00:25:09,158
Do you have your period?

454
00:25:12,245 --> 00:25:13,996
I don't want to fight, okay?

455
00:25:14,997 --> 00:25:17,959
But we've been together
for six years, Manny.

456
00:25:27,093 --> 00:25:28,636
Why aren't you answering my calls?

457
00:25:29,095 --> 00:25:30,095
<i>Sorry, babe.</i>

458
00:25:31,996 --> 00:25:32,996
You failed?

459
00:25:34,684 --> 00:25:35,684
Where are you now?

460
00:25:35,893 --> 00:25:36,893
<i>I’m eating.</i>

461
00:25:37,822 --> 00:25:41,826
<i>I'm thinking about finally starting
my bike tour around the country.</i>

462
00:25:42,608 --> 00:25:44,193
Do you have time for that?

463
00:25:44,717 --> 00:25:45,757
<i>I’m going for a bike ride.</i>

464
00:25:46,362 --> 00:25:47,697
<i>To clear my head.</i>

465
00:25:49,490 --> 00:25:50,699
What are you trying to
clear your head from?

466
00:25:50,700 --> 00:25:53,244
You didn't even use your brain
to pass your exams.

467
00:26:00,174 --> 00:26:02,301
He’s such a headache!

468
00:26:03,004 --> 00:26:06,257
I was actually going to treat him
to his favorite <i>sisig</i> to celebrate.

469
00:26:08,301 --> 00:26:10,970
Lord, what am I going to do?

470
00:26:12,388 --> 00:26:13,639
Hey! Wait!

471
00:26:15,099 --> 00:26:16,601
Are you sure you don't want a ride?

472
00:26:17,101 --> 00:26:18,519
I’m in a rush.

473
00:26:18,853 --> 00:26:19,645
Is that so?

474
00:26:19,646 --> 00:26:21,397
Alright, since it's my treat today,

475
00:26:22,064 --> 00:26:23,649
drinks are on you this Friday.

476
00:26:23,774 --> 00:26:24,650
So, what do you say?

477
00:26:24,775 --> 00:26:25,818
I know a cheap place.

478
00:26:27,153 --> 00:26:29,530
Let's just say the coffee was on me.

479
00:26:30,072 --> 00:26:32,283
So, you don't need to
buy me drinks on Friday.

480
00:26:32,366 --> 00:26:33,366
Okay?

481
00:26:33,868 --> 00:26:35,286
Let's go now, sir.

482
00:26:35,780 --> 00:26:37,329
How about your number?
Your cellphone number!

483
00:26:37,330 --> 00:26:38,748
Your cellphone number!

484
00:26:51,542 --> 00:26:52,251
<i>Hanz...</i>

485
00:26:52,276 --> 00:26:53,151
What’s up?

486
00:26:53,176 --> 00:26:54,177
<i>Where are you?</i>

487
00:26:54,764 --> 00:26:55,764
<i>Have lunch with me.</i>

488
00:26:56,182 --> 00:26:57,182
No way!

489
00:26:57,850 --> 00:26:58,850
<i>My treat.</i>

490
00:27:00,102 --> 00:27:01,102
Your treat?

491
00:27:01,145 --> 00:27:02,145
<i>Yes.</i>

492
00:27:02,773 --> 00:27:05,192
If it’s your treat, I’m going.

493
00:27:09,913 --> 00:27:11,498
Thank you for the lunch.

494
00:27:11,906 --> 00:27:13,699
Wow, you even got me dessert!

495
00:27:14,992 --> 00:27:16,535
Why did you treat me, anyway?

496
00:27:16,952 --> 00:27:19,080
Did Rob pass?

497
00:27:24,335 --> 00:27:25,419
Did he pass?

498
00:27:28,090 --> 00:27:29,428
I knew it.

499
00:27:30,220 --> 00:27:31,569
That idiot didn't pass.

500
00:27:33,094 --> 00:27:34,887
Well, as always,

501
00:27:35,388 --> 00:27:37,181
your boyfriend is always such a burden.

502
00:27:38,391 --> 00:27:39,391
Wait.

503
00:27:40,017 --> 00:27:41,894
Has he paid you the deposit yet?

504
00:27:43,229 --> 00:27:44,563
He’ll pay eventually.

505
00:27:45,272 --> 00:27:46,315
Are you sure?

506
00:27:46,816 --> 00:27:48,108
You already have so many varicose veins

507
00:27:48,109 --> 00:27:50,820
from standing at the mall
every day just to support him.

508
00:27:51,612 --> 00:27:53,030
If he had any conscience,

509
00:27:53,531 --> 00:27:55,491
he’d at least get a side job
and earn some money.

510
00:27:56,242 --> 00:27:57,242
Hey!

511
00:27:57,493 --> 00:27:59,285
Stop insulting my boyfriend.

512
00:27:59,286 --> 00:28:01,729
Besides, I don't want him working.

513
00:28:03,374 --> 00:28:04,374
Wow.

514
00:28:05,042 --> 00:28:06,377
Are you a martyr?

515
00:28:07,712 --> 00:28:10,089
I can't believe there are still
martyrs these days.

516
00:28:11,382 --> 00:28:12,758
You're so annoying!

517
00:28:13,217 --> 00:28:14,176
I should've never treated you!

518
00:28:14,177 --> 00:28:15,343
- Give that to me!
- No, don’t!

519
00:28:15,344 --> 00:28:16,220
Don’t worry about it.

520
00:28:16,221 --> 00:28:17,388
No, really. It's okay.

521
00:28:17,805 --> 00:28:19,645
You already gave it to me.
Don’t take it back.

522
00:28:24,770 --> 00:28:26,522
<i>There he goes again.</i>

523
00:28:28,774 --> 00:28:30,525
<i>You really won't leave me alone, will you?</i>

524
00:28:30,526 --> 00:28:32,486
Hey.

525
00:28:33,112 --> 00:28:34,155
Stay close to me.

526
00:28:36,991 --> 00:28:38,033
Sit beside me.

527
00:28:38,534 --> 00:28:39,534
Hmm?

528
00:28:41,370 --> 00:28:42,370
Why should I?

529
00:28:42,629 --> 00:28:43,880
Just stay close to me.

530
00:28:44,373 --> 00:28:45,373
What?

531
00:28:45,398 --> 00:28:46,148
Here you go.

532
00:28:46,173 --> 00:28:46,799
Closer!

533
00:28:46,824 --> 00:28:47,824
There.

534
00:28:47,918 --> 00:28:49,587
Are you that disgusted?

535
00:28:49,754 --> 00:28:50,379
What?

536
00:28:50,404 --> 00:28:52,406
Stay closer, come on.

537
00:28:55,134 --> 00:28:56,510
- There!
- There you go!

538
00:28:58,978 --> 00:29:00,355
That’s it!

539
00:29:00,848 --> 00:29:02,041
Put your arm around me.

540
00:29:02,266 --> 00:29:03,266
What?!

541
00:29:03,476 --> 00:29:04,643
Put your arm around me.

542
00:29:04,769 --> 00:29:05,811
Embrace?

543
00:29:06,437 --> 00:29:07,563
You're making this so hard.

544
00:29:08,628 --> 00:29:09,837
What’s the matter with you?

545
00:29:11,901 --> 00:29:13,235
Over my shoulder.

546
00:29:15,780 --> 00:29:16,780
Come on.

547
00:29:18,574 --> 00:29:19,574
Like this?

548
00:29:20,512 --> 00:29:22,512
Where is it? I can't feel it.
Place it over there!

549
00:29:36,763 --> 00:29:37,889
Pat my head.

550
00:29:39,427 --> 00:29:40,595
Touch my hair.

551
00:29:40,793 --> 00:29:41,627
Hold on.

552
00:29:41,787 --> 00:29:43,247
What’s wrong with you?

553
00:29:44,391 --> 00:29:46,143
Don't you watch K-dramas?

554
00:29:46,533 --> 00:29:48,451
You know, when the
guy pats the girl's head.

555
00:29:49,230 --> 00:29:50,356
Pat my head.

556
00:29:51,982 --> 00:29:53,108
I don’t want to.

557
00:29:53,317 --> 00:29:54,443
Come on, pat it.

558
00:29:54,652 --> 00:29:56,236
- I got that for you.
- It’s sticky.

559
00:29:56,237 --> 00:29:57,363
Do it!

560
00:30:07,373 --> 00:30:08,582
Pat it.

561
00:30:10,125 --> 00:30:11,125
Pat it.

562
00:30:11,126 --> 00:30:11,794
Pat?

563
00:30:11,795 --> 00:30:13,128
Yes. Pat.

564
00:30:34,066 --> 00:30:35,359
It’s so sticky!

565
00:30:37,152 --> 00:30:38,445
It's so sticky!

566
00:30:38,779 --> 00:30:40,573
I said pat, don't pull my hair!

567
00:30:41,490 --> 00:30:42,575
Did you take a shower?

568
00:30:42,867 --> 00:30:44,027
That's none of your business.

569
00:30:44,451 --> 00:30:45,451
Go leave.

570
00:30:45,536 --> 00:30:46,829
You messed up my hair!

571
00:30:51,292 --> 00:30:52,459
You’re so dramatic.

572
00:31:02,836 --> 00:31:05,255
Good thing this was 50% off.

573
00:31:07,135 --> 00:31:08,267
I hope he likes it.

574
00:31:16,963 --> 00:31:18,840
He hasn't been answering for a while now.

575
00:31:20,314 --> 00:31:21,649
I’ll just surprise him.

576
00:31:24,366 --> 00:31:25,576
Hey! Hello!

577
00:31:25,966 --> 00:31:26,966
Room 3?

578
00:31:27,578 --> 00:31:28,495
Room 3!

579
00:31:28,496 --> 00:31:30,414
Room 3!

580
00:31:31,248 --> 00:31:32,458
What happened to him?

581
00:31:48,307 --> 00:31:49,474
Hey, bros!

582
00:31:49,475 --> 00:31:50,476
Clean that up!

583
00:31:50,935 --> 00:31:51,976
Room 3 is here!

584
00:31:51,977 --> 00:31:52,603
Faster!

585
00:31:52,603 --> 00:31:53,520
Dude! Go knock on Rob’s door!

586
00:31:53,520 --> 00:31:53,896
Hurry!

587
00:31:53,897 --> 00:31:55,147
Faster!

588
00:31:59,944 --> 00:32:01,111
Rob! Rob!

589
00:32:01,862 --> 00:32:02,863
Room 3 is here!

590
00:32:35,479 --> 00:32:35,938
Hey.

591
00:32:36,313 --> 00:32:37,313
Babe!

592
00:32:37,606 --> 00:32:38,606
Babe!

593
00:32:39,525 --> 00:32:40,067
Babe!

594
00:32:40,068 --> 00:32:41,235
Come, let’s eat!

595
00:32:41,443 --> 00:32:42,820
Hi, Room 3!

596
00:32:43,364 --> 00:32:45,699
Babe, why aren’t you answering my calls?

597
00:32:46,281 --> 00:32:47,281
Oh...

598
00:32:47,324 --> 00:32:48,324
Well...

599
00:32:49,201 --> 00:32:52,830
Sorry, I left my phone in the room.

600
00:32:53,580 --> 00:32:54,580
Hmm...

601
00:32:55,541 --> 00:32:56,541
This is for you.

602
00:32:58,669 --> 00:33:00,087
What’s the bike for?

603
00:33:00,546 --> 00:33:03,048
You don't even know
how to ride a bike, do you?

604
00:33:04,497 --> 00:33:06,933
I thought you wanted to go on a
bike tour around the Philippines?

605
00:33:07,005 --> 00:33:09,165
Don't tell me you're planning
to use that broken bike?

606
00:33:09,896 --> 00:33:10,897
You’re right.

607
00:33:11,803 --> 00:33:12,803
But...

608
00:33:13,517 --> 00:33:15,936
You don't need to buy one.

609
00:33:16,603 --> 00:33:17,730
That's a waste of money.

610
00:33:18,230 --> 00:33:20,149
Besides, what kind of bike is this?

611
00:33:21,692 --> 00:33:23,485
So this is just an XC bike?

612
00:33:24,486 --> 00:33:25,611
Will you stop?

613
00:33:25,612 --> 00:33:27,448
I even left work early just to buy that.

614
00:33:27,990 --> 00:33:28,907
No, I'm just kidding.

615
00:33:28,949 --> 00:33:30,117
Come on, let's eat.

616
00:33:32,244 --> 00:33:33,244
Hey!

617
00:33:33,269 --> 00:33:34,629
Your jogging pants are inside out.

618
00:33:37,624 --> 00:33:38,624
Huh?

619
00:33:41,128 --> 00:33:42,128
Oh...

620
00:33:43,213 --> 00:33:44,422
You're not yourself today.

621
00:33:44,423 --> 00:33:45,423
Pull yourself together!

622
00:33:46,592 --> 00:33:49,094
Oh, aren't you the one who sells <i>bulalo</i>?

623
00:33:49,678 --> 00:33:50,596
Where are you selling now?

624
00:33:50,597 --> 00:33:52,037
You're no longer at your usual spot.

625
00:33:53,307 --> 00:33:55,142
Oh, do you deliver now?

626
00:33:55,684 --> 00:33:58,020
Yes, it helps us make more money.

627
00:33:59,271 --> 00:33:59,938
Oh...

628
00:34:00,064 --> 00:34:02,024
You really brought the whole pot with you.

629
00:34:03,192 --> 00:34:03,817
Yeah.

630
00:34:03,842 --> 00:34:05,677
But your <i>bulalo</i> really is the best!

631
00:34:06,028 --> 00:34:07,696
It’s actually my boyfriend’s favorite.

632
00:34:07,988 --> 00:34:09,031
Could I have some, please?

633
00:34:09,656 --> 00:34:11,200
Oh yes, sure.

634
00:34:13,381 --> 00:34:14,381
Oh no!

635
00:34:14,984 --> 00:34:16,694
Your hands must be getting tired.

636
00:34:19,496 --> 00:34:20,496
Serpentine?

637
00:34:27,165 --> 00:34:28,708
That serpentine hair tie of yours,

638
00:34:30,260 --> 00:34:31,720
it looks just like mine.

639
00:34:41,355 --> 00:34:43,440
Why is it that the clothes you're wearing,

640
00:34:44,828 --> 00:34:46,735
it matches my boyfriend’s pants?

641
00:34:54,451 --> 00:34:56,411
Isn't this the perfume I gave you?

642
00:35:17,307 --> 00:35:19,101
I knew it!

643
00:35:19,643 --> 00:35:20,643
Get over here!

644
00:35:20,894 --> 00:35:24,773
Help!

645
00:35:24,982 --> 00:35:25,982
Get over here!

646
00:35:26,942 --> 00:35:27,985
How dare you!

647
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:50,132
Didn't you give me this bag
as a gift last year?

648
00:35:53,906 --> 00:35:56,033
This is my very first designer bag.

649
00:36:00,642 --> 00:36:02,728
I even got mad at you
for spending so much money.

650
00:36:06,273 --> 00:36:08,108
But when you gave this to me, you said...

651
00:36:12,112 --> 00:36:14,114
we'd get married once
you passed your exams.

652
00:36:18,827 --> 00:36:19,995
Yes.

653
00:36:22,581 --> 00:36:24,416
But I keep failing.

654
00:36:28,962 --> 00:36:30,964
Rob, I trusted you.

655
00:36:46,730 --> 00:36:48,148
I’m sorry.

656
00:36:53,195 --> 00:36:54,696
I’m really sorry, Aira.

657
00:36:55,530 --> 00:36:56,573
You know what...

658
00:36:58,533 --> 00:37:00,535
You know what,
I don't mind if you keep failing.

659
00:37:01,787 --> 00:37:03,622
I was already ready to
just take care of you.

660
00:37:06,625 --> 00:37:07,709
Hey!

661
00:37:09,294 --> 00:37:11,088
Kneel in front of her.

662
00:37:19,888 --> 00:37:21,181
Sorry, Aira.

663
00:37:21,473 --> 00:37:22,683
I’m really sorry.

664
00:37:24,559 --> 00:37:25,559
Did you think…

665
00:37:26,603 --> 00:37:29,690
Did you think I was making millions?

666
00:37:30,607 --> 00:37:33,609
Just because I'm the one
paying your monthly deposit?

667
00:37:33,610 --> 00:37:35,070
Even your allowance.

668
00:37:37,948 --> 00:37:39,116
Maybe...

669
00:37:40,993 --> 00:37:42,995
Maybe I could understand if…

670
00:37:43,287 --> 00:37:45,289
If you had left me for someone younger

671
00:37:45,580 --> 00:37:47,582
or richer, but…

672
00:37:48,959 --> 00:37:54,047
You replaced me for an old woman
who owns a small eatery?

673
00:37:56,341 --> 00:37:57,676
Excuse me.

674
00:37:58,260 --> 00:38:00,262
It's not that small anymore.

675
00:38:02,222 --> 00:38:04,807
Yes! My restaurant is packed again!

676
00:38:04,808 --> 00:38:06,809
And my loyal customers are here again!

677
00:38:06,810 --> 00:38:08,812
And you're in for a delicious meal!

678
00:38:09,021 --> 00:38:14,443
Of course!
Welcome to <i>Queen of Bulalo</i>!

679
00:38:14,818 --> 00:38:17,987
<i>Bulalo! Bulalo!</i>

680
00:38:17,988 --> 00:38:19,990
<i>Queen of Bulalo, </i>my ass!

681
00:38:21,283 --> 00:38:23,285
Rob isn't as stupid as I thought.

682
00:38:24,870 --> 00:38:28,749
See? Didn't I tell you it
wasn't small anymore?

683
00:38:30,334 --> 00:38:31,710
Oh, dear!

684
00:38:32,002 --> 00:38:34,004
So, have you packed your things yet?

685
00:38:34,171 --> 00:38:35,422
- You’re all sweaty!
- Oh, yeah.

686
00:38:35,630 --> 00:38:38,175
And I’ve already booked my accommodation.

687
00:38:38,425 --> 00:38:40,427
I was thinking I could just use the bike.

688
00:38:40,677 --> 00:38:42,679
So I might not use the car anymore.

689
00:38:43,055 --> 00:38:43,597
Huh?

690
00:38:43,889 --> 00:38:46,390
No, it's fine.
You can just use the car.

691
00:38:46,391 --> 00:38:47,892
That car isn't really important anyway.

692
00:38:47,893 --> 00:38:52,647
What matters is you.
You're what's important.

693
00:38:54,066 --> 00:38:55,692
So that's why you didn't want my bike.

694
00:38:56,526 --> 00:38:58,152
Is that an XC bike too?

695
00:38:58,153 --> 00:38:59,320
Uh, no.

696
00:38:59,321 --> 00:39:00,863
High-end trail bike.

697
00:39:00,864 --> 00:39:02,866
And it has more gears, too.

698
00:39:04,701 --> 00:39:06,786
Oh, by the way, Aira.

699
00:39:06,787 --> 00:39:09,080
I've been wanting to give this
to you for a long time.

700
00:39:09,081 --> 00:39:13,001
This is the security
deposit for Rob's apartment.

701
00:39:14,977 --> 00:39:16,979
Are you trying to bribe me
because I caught you?

702
00:39:17,547 --> 00:39:20,841
It's not like that.
Come on, just take it.

703
00:39:20,842 --> 00:39:22,552
Come on.

704
00:39:23,512 --> 00:39:27,265
Would you like us to
give you a ride instead?

705
00:39:27,974 --> 00:39:30,893
Yes! Besides, your bike is so heavy!

706
00:39:30,894 --> 00:39:32,896
Come on, let's load this into the car.

707
00:39:32,921 --> 00:39:35,507
Ahh! Ouch!

708
00:39:36,942 --> 00:39:38,485
What are you doing, huh?!

709
00:39:38,735 --> 00:39:39,861
What’s wrong with you?!

710
00:39:41,571 --> 00:39:42,963
This is mine!

711
00:39:43,156 --> 00:39:44,449
I'm just taking it back!

712
00:39:45,158 --> 00:39:46,284
Taxi!

713
00:39:48,116 --> 00:39:50,452
That won't fit, ma'am!
You'll need a truck!

714
00:39:53,250 --> 00:39:54,543
Aira!

715
00:39:56,336 --> 00:39:57,754
Hop in!

716
00:40:18,191 --> 00:40:19,234
Here.

717
00:40:20,235 --> 00:40:23,237
I said <i>kikiam</i>, not <i>kwek-kwek</i>!

718
00:40:23,238 --> 00:40:25,240
You need protein, not carbs.

719
00:40:26,450 --> 00:40:28,452
Coach, why are you meddling with my diet?

720
00:40:29,369 --> 00:40:32,122
Once a coach, forever a coach.

721
00:40:32,497 --> 00:40:36,126
Once a martial artist,
forever a martial artist.

722
00:40:36,832 --> 00:40:41,648
You need to stay in shape
in case you ever make a comeback.

723
00:40:41,673 --> 00:40:43,008
Come back?

724
00:40:43,675 --> 00:40:47,596
Coach, who told you I
was making a comeback?

725
00:40:47,679 --> 00:40:49,389
Why? Did I say it was you?

726
00:40:50,015 --> 00:40:51,308
Coach, be honest with me.

727
00:40:51,558 --> 00:40:54,603
The other day, you were hanging
around near my house.

728
00:40:54,978 --> 00:40:57,731
And now you're going to hang around
near my workplace, too?

729
00:40:59,357 --> 00:41:00,357
Coach...

730
00:41:00,942 --> 00:41:02,903
No matter what you do…

731
00:41:03,236 --> 00:41:06,281
I will never go back to Taekwondo.

732
00:41:07,240 --> 00:41:09,159
I’ll be turning thirty in just a few years.

733
00:41:09,868 --> 00:41:11,453
I’m too old to join the National Team.

734
00:41:11,828 --> 00:41:12,828
Hold on!

735
00:41:13,038 --> 00:41:15,248
Who said anything about Taekwondo?

736
00:41:16,041 --> 00:41:18,502
When it comes to MMA,
you're still young.

737
00:41:19,085 --> 00:41:21,962
It'd be a shame to let that
roundhouse kick go to waste.

738
00:41:21,963 --> 00:41:23,215
Roundhouse kick.

739
00:41:23,965 --> 00:41:25,425
Coach, it’s been long gone.

740
00:41:25,926 --> 00:41:27,385
Let it rest in peace.

741
00:41:28,178 --> 00:41:29,763
Besides, it's just a hassle.

742
00:41:30,472 --> 00:41:32,557
It just makes me lose my confidence.

743
00:41:33,808 --> 00:41:35,143
That was a long time ago, Hanz.

744
00:41:35,435 --> 00:41:36,603
You should move on.

745
00:41:37,687 --> 00:41:39,564
Don’t you miss competing?

746
00:41:48,657 --> 00:41:51,371
Alright. You can go.

747
00:41:52,744 --> 00:41:54,019
No.

748
00:41:54,621 --> 00:41:56,164
I’ll eat here instead.

749
00:41:56,414 --> 00:41:57,414
Give that to me.

750
00:42:26,279 --> 00:42:27,280
<i>This is embarrassing.</i>

751
00:42:28,238 --> 00:42:29,990
<i>I just wanted the ground to swallow me up.</i>

752
00:42:31,533 --> 00:42:33,326
<i>Why am I so pathetic?</i>

753
00:42:34,077 --> 00:42:35,661
For celebrity news…

754
00:42:35,662 --> 00:42:39,373
Former celebrity broadcaster
Julia Villegas announced

755
00:42:39,374 --> 00:42:41,000
an official statement

756
00:42:41,001 --> 00:42:44,503
announcing her separation
from her husband, Geofry Lee,

757
00:42:44,504 --> 00:42:46,673
after three years of marriage.

758
00:42:47,173 --> 00:42:50,968
It will be recalled that the
famous journalist resigned from her career…

759
00:42:51,019 --> 00:42:53,804
and decided to settle down abroad

760
00:42:53,805 --> 00:42:57,309
after marrying Lee, a business tycoon.

761
00:42:57,642 --> 00:43:00,436
This unexpected turn of
events came as a shock

762
00:43:00,437 --> 00:43:04,148
as there had been no reports of
any conflict between the two.

763
00:43:04,149 --> 00:43:08,861
We are currently trying to get
a comment from both parties.

764
00:43:08,862 --> 00:43:12,115
However, no official statement
has been released from either party.

765
00:43:12,324 --> 00:43:15,159
Julia and Geofry got
married in the United States

766
00:43:15,160 --> 00:43:18,580
where divorce is legal and permitted.

767
00:43:18,997 --> 00:43:20,582
She’s the businessman's wife, right?

768
00:43:20,999 --> 00:43:23,335
What happened to Ms.
Julia Villegas’s husband?

769
00:43:28,715 --> 00:43:29,799
<i>Julia?</i>

770
00:43:30,717 --> 00:43:32,010
<i>So she's separated now.</i>

771
00:43:33,595 --> 00:43:35,395
But didn't they have
their marriage annulled?

772
00:43:36,890 --> 00:43:37,557
I have no idea.

773
00:43:37,557 --> 00:43:38,557
Annulment?

774
00:43:39,184 --> 00:43:39,976
Let me see!

775
00:43:39,977 --> 00:43:40,977
Hey! Wait!
What do you want?!

776
00:43:40,978 --> 00:43:42,938
- Let me see!
- We're going to get into an accident!

777
00:43:44,939 --> 00:43:46,608
Watch out! Someone's there!

778
00:43:47,150 --> 00:43:48,818
What the hell!

779
00:43:54,032 --> 00:43:55,075
Are you okay?

780
00:43:55,700 --> 00:43:56,700
Huh?

781
00:43:57,369 --> 00:43:59,913
Rob! We hit someone!

782
00:44:00,413 --> 00:44:01,413
Hold on!

783
00:44:02,332 --> 00:44:03,332
Let me check.

784
00:44:05,168 --> 00:44:06,168
Oh my gosh.

785
00:44:08,171 --> 00:44:09,964
Oh! We really did hit someone!

786
00:44:10,090 --> 00:44:12,050
Oh, my! I'm so sorry!

787
00:44:12,175 --> 00:44:13,926
Sir, we didn't see you!

788
00:44:13,927 --> 00:44:15,302
Please forgive us!

789
00:44:15,303 --> 00:44:16,805
Didn't you see the red light?

790
00:44:24,020 --> 00:44:24,521
Hey!

791
00:44:24,521 --> 00:44:25,271
Oh my gosh, are you okay?

792
00:44:25,271 --> 00:44:26,271
Are you okay?

793
00:44:27,482 --> 00:44:28,316
Rob?

794
00:44:28,316 --> 00:44:29,316
Hanz?

795
00:44:31,444 --> 00:44:33,321
Oh, it's you!
Are you going to see Aira?

796
00:44:34,614 --> 00:44:36,741
How did you manage to buy a car?

797
00:44:38,118 --> 00:44:39,536
Do you two know each other?

798
00:44:43,873 --> 00:44:45,249
What? Are you okay?

799
00:44:45,250 --> 00:44:46,291
- Did you get hit?
- I’m fine.

800
00:44:46,292 --> 00:44:47,460
I’m not hurt.

801
00:44:47,919 --> 00:44:49,002
Sorry.

802
00:44:49,003 --> 00:44:49,629
Ouch!

803
00:44:49,629 --> 00:44:50,505
Easy, easy.

804
00:44:50,506 --> 00:44:51,798
Don’t stand up!

805
00:44:53,675 --> 00:44:56,344
Aira, I see you two are together.

806
00:44:57,303 --> 00:44:58,471
I’m fine.

807
00:44:58,722 --> 00:45:00,889
You know, we're practically family here...

808
00:45:00,890 --> 00:45:01,933
Will you just shut up?!

809
00:45:02,642 --> 00:45:03,810
Call the police.

810
00:45:04,185 --> 00:45:06,105
Go to the hospital and
get yourself checked out.

811
00:45:09,816 --> 00:45:11,025
Did you two have a fight?

812
00:45:11,735 --> 00:45:14,446
Well, you know. It's a long story.

813
00:45:15,864 --> 00:45:17,407
Sorry, who is she again?

814
00:45:17,490 --> 00:45:18,491
Your aunt?

815
00:45:21,327 --> 00:45:22,954
She’s the mother of that jerk’s child.

816
00:45:23,913 --> 00:45:25,457
Oh, she’s Rob’s mom!

817
00:45:27,125 --> 00:45:29,501
Mother, I'm sorry we had to meet
under these circumstances.

818
00:45:29,502 --> 00:45:30,502
This is so funny.

819
00:45:31,296 --> 00:45:32,380
I’m Hanz.

820
00:45:32,922 --> 00:45:34,048
Nice to meet you.

821
00:45:36,593 --> 00:45:38,303
That old woman is pregnant!

822
00:45:40,036 --> 00:45:41,454
She's carrying their baby!

823
00:45:44,058 --> 00:45:46,408
All the money I've been giving him,

824
00:45:48,605 --> 00:45:51,674
he’s been spending it on meals
at that woman’s restaurant!

825
00:45:56,446 --> 00:45:58,239
They see each other all the time.

826
00:45:58,782 --> 00:46:00,867
They even have meals together.

827
00:46:03,387 --> 00:46:07,516
And now they have a child together!

828
00:46:15,673 --> 00:46:17,090
- Hey, think about it —
- You bastard!

829
00:46:17,091 --> 00:46:17,926
Hey, wait a minute!

830
00:46:17,926 --> 00:46:18,885
I will kill you!

831
00:46:18,886 --> 00:46:20,136
Get your hands off Rob!

832
00:46:21,054 --> 00:46:22,054
Oh, for goodness’ sake!

833
00:46:23,556 --> 00:46:26,142
Get your hands off him!
Let go of him!

834
00:46:26,559 --> 00:46:27,769
Stop it!

835
00:46:28,353 --> 00:46:30,104
Wait! Stop it!

836
00:46:30,730 --> 00:46:31,815
Stop it!

837
00:46:36,194 --> 00:46:38,363
Wasn’t that given to you
by your asshole ex?

838
00:46:38,912 --> 00:46:40,312
Why don't you just throw that away?

839
00:46:41,407 --> 00:46:42,575
This is branded.

840
00:46:43,368 --> 00:46:47,163
I’ll have it fixed tomorrow and
sell it so I can treat you to some drinks.

841
00:46:47,997 --> 00:46:49,499
You’re really crazy.

842
00:46:50,208 --> 00:46:51,292
By the way,

843
00:46:51,831 --> 00:46:55,251
was that old lady some kind of amazon?

844
00:46:55,880 --> 00:46:57,422
She was strong!

845
00:46:57,423 --> 00:46:59,174
Why did you attack Rob in the first place?

846
00:46:59,175 --> 00:47:02,136
And did you really do Taekwondo?

847
00:47:02,846 --> 00:47:06,015
Well, I couldn't exactly kick
the pregnant woman, could I?

848
00:47:07,183 --> 00:47:08,059
Right?

849
00:47:08,059 --> 00:47:08,601
Wait!

850
00:47:08,643 --> 00:47:09,643
Oh!

851
00:47:10,520 --> 00:47:11,979
What’s the matter with you?

852
00:47:11,980 --> 00:47:13,481
What’s going on with your life?

853
00:47:15,358 --> 00:47:16,901
Just mind your own business.

854
00:47:17,585 --> 00:47:19,045
Let’s just say,

855
00:47:19,524 --> 00:47:20,964
I was the one who broke up with him.

856
00:47:22,115 --> 00:47:23,616
By the way,

857
00:47:24,576 --> 00:47:27,328
have you heard about Julia’s annulment?

858
00:47:34,794 --> 00:47:35,794
Hey!

859
00:47:36,170 --> 00:47:37,213
Look at this guy!

860
00:47:37,547 --> 00:47:38,547
Ouch!

861
00:47:47,348 --> 00:47:48,892
I have the worst luck.

862
00:47:56,149 --> 00:47:58,735
This is so frustrating!

863
00:48:02,363 --> 00:48:06,075
Look what happened to my shoes!
They’re all I have!

864
00:48:07,619 --> 00:48:12,165
My luck is terrible!
Why does this happen to me?

865
00:48:16,044 --> 00:48:18,379
My luck just keeps getting worse!

866
00:48:23,217 --> 00:48:27,138
I already told you not to buy fake shoes.

867
00:48:28,306 --> 00:48:30,600
There are plenty of cheap ones
with good quality.

868
00:48:33,186 --> 00:48:36,188
What are you doing?!
Don't throw my shoes away!

869
00:48:36,189 --> 00:48:38,441
Stop crying!

870
00:48:38,691 --> 00:48:40,568
Aira, I'm getting annoyed with you.

871
00:48:42,987 --> 00:48:44,780
Your shoes are broken!
Your bag is broken!

872
00:48:44,781 --> 00:48:46,699
Your whole life is a mess, Aira!

873
00:48:47,050 --> 00:48:48,927
I’m the one good thing
you’ve got left.

874
00:48:49,285 --> 00:48:50,285
Huh?

875
00:48:53,414 --> 00:48:54,414
Nothing.

876
00:48:56,644 --> 00:48:57,644
Let’s go.

877
00:49:01,172 --> 00:49:02,172
Come on!

878
00:49:02,674 --> 00:49:03,840
Where are you going?

879
00:49:03,841 --> 00:49:05,426
Let’s go. I’ll buy you something.

880
00:49:05,593 --> 00:49:06,052
Wait.

881
00:49:06,053 --> 00:49:07,804
Stop it!
Don’t get it anymore!

882
00:49:11,182 --> 00:49:12,350
It’s dirty.

883
00:49:21,317 --> 00:49:22,485
You're going to buy me a bag?

884
00:49:22,944 --> 00:49:23,987
Of course.

885
00:49:24,404 --> 00:49:25,446
Check this out.

886
00:49:25,780 --> 00:49:26,780
Miss...

887
00:49:27,448 --> 00:49:29,867
Simple, yet nice.

888
00:49:29,951 --> 00:49:31,953
That's a new arrival, one-fifty.

889
00:49:32,078 --> 00:49:33,078
Oh, one fif...

890
00:49:33,955 --> 00:49:36,164
And look, you can even put stones on this

891
00:49:36,165 --> 00:49:38,084
and then use it to smack people like Rob.

892
00:49:40,128 --> 00:49:41,128
Hanz...

893
00:49:41,352 --> 00:49:44,772
You know what, I'm going to use
that bag until the day I die.

894
00:49:46,259 --> 00:49:47,427
You don't have to.

895
00:49:48,261 --> 00:49:51,472
And by the way, you can
pick out some shoes too.

896
00:49:53,808 --> 00:49:54,808
Seriously?

897
00:49:58,855 --> 00:49:59,855
Hmm...

898
00:50:09,449 --> 00:50:10,992
Oh, okay!

899
00:50:13,074 --> 00:50:14,077
Miss...

900
00:50:15,204 --> 00:50:16,205
How much?

901
00:50:16,507 --> 00:50:19,218
One fifty plus two hundred,
three fifty.

902
00:50:20,460 --> 00:50:21,460
No discount?

903
00:50:26,257 --> 00:50:27,508
You can’t take it back.

904
00:50:28,584 --> 00:50:29,752
Yeah, I won’t.

905
00:50:38,853 --> 00:50:40,063
You’re something else.

906
00:50:41,564 --> 00:50:42,564
Why?

907
00:50:42,690 --> 00:50:43,858
Is that comfortable?

908
00:50:44,520 --> 00:50:45,520
Mhm!

909
00:50:45,964 --> 00:50:46,964
Even this bag.

910
00:50:47,195 --> 00:50:48,738
This can hold five bottles of booze.

911
00:50:49,113 --> 00:50:49,781
Hey!

912
00:50:49,947 --> 00:50:52,467
I didn’t buy that for you
just so you could fill it with booze.

913
00:50:54,994 --> 00:50:55,994
You know what,

914
00:50:56,370 --> 00:51:00,625
never in my life did I imagine
you’d actually buy a bag for a woman.

915
00:51:02,347 --> 00:51:03,376
How’s that?

916
00:51:03,419 --> 00:51:04,462
How’s that smile again?

917
00:51:04,962 --> 00:51:05,962
Can I see?

918
00:51:07,465 --> 00:51:08,465
That’s it!

919
00:51:08,966 --> 00:51:10,967
That’s what you should’ve done earlier!

920
00:51:10,968 --> 00:51:12,428
It’s so romantic when you do that!

921
00:51:23,314 --> 00:51:24,674
Does this make your heart flutter?

922
00:51:26,651 --> 00:51:27,651
Oh...

923
00:51:27,735 --> 00:51:29,112
Why would I feel giddy?

924
00:51:29,695 --> 00:51:31,197
Then, why are you blushing?

925
00:51:32,281 --> 00:51:33,281
See...

926
00:51:38,162 --> 00:51:39,330
Am I blushing?

927
00:51:42,959 --> 00:51:43,959
No.

928
00:51:45,086 --> 00:51:47,338
Maybe because of the alcohol.

929
00:51:48,714 --> 00:51:50,550
You really need to stop drinking.

930
00:51:50,883 --> 00:51:52,363
So you won't get all flushed anymore.

931
00:51:53,261 --> 00:51:54,262
Is that so?

932
00:51:55,346 --> 00:51:56,597
It’s because of the alcohol?

933
00:52:02,562 --> 00:52:05,189
<i>Why is my heart beating so fast?</i>

934
00:52:16,701 --> 00:52:18,536
Isn’t this the perfume I gave you?

935
00:52:21,164 --> 00:52:22,582
Let him go!

936
00:53:03,998 --> 00:53:05,999
Hey, stop it!

937
00:53:06,000 --> 00:53:08,127
Susie, she won’t stop
unless you put an end to it!

938
00:53:08,502 --> 00:53:09,629
Aira, stop it!

939
00:53:09,837 --> 00:53:10,671
Ahh!

940
00:53:10,796 --> 00:53:11,964
It hurts, Hanz.

941
00:53:12,298 --> 00:53:13,965
She scratched me!

942
00:53:13,966 --> 00:53:15,009
What? Can I see?

943
00:53:16,302 --> 00:53:17,928
Why did you scratch her?

944
00:53:17,929 --> 00:53:19,305
She was the one who started it!

945
00:53:19,555 --> 00:53:21,057
I got hurt too!

946
00:53:21,224 --> 00:53:22,266
It hurts.

947
00:53:22,433 --> 00:53:23,100
Let me see.

948
00:53:23,101 --> 00:53:24,142
It hurts.

949
00:53:24,143 --> 00:53:27,188
Why start a fight when
you know you can't win?

950
00:53:27,654 --> 00:53:28,654
Right?

951
00:53:29,106 --> 00:53:30,607
It hurts.

952
00:53:30,608 --> 00:53:31,775
Let’s go see a doctor.

953
00:53:31,776 --> 00:53:32,943
That needs to be checked.

954
00:53:32,944 --> 00:53:34,486
Let’s go.

955
00:53:34,487 --> 00:53:35,529
Aira, let’s go!

956
00:53:49,877 --> 00:53:51,419
Hey! Sorry!

957
00:53:51,420 --> 00:53:52,712
Can you throw this as well?

958
00:53:52,713 --> 00:53:53,839
You always do this.

959
00:53:54,101 --> 00:53:55,101
Oh, wow!

960
00:53:55,126 --> 00:53:56,168
How annoying!

961
00:53:56,412 --> 00:53:58,039
Take out the trash, babe.

962
00:53:59,438 --> 00:54:00,480
What “babe”?

963
00:54:00,638 --> 00:54:02,723
What “babe”?
Why are you calling me “babe”?

964
00:54:02,791 --> 00:54:04,491
That sounds awful, Aira.

965
00:54:05,184 --> 00:54:06,184
Fine.

966
00:54:09,188 --> 00:54:10,606
Thank you, babe.

967
00:54:10,650 --> 00:54:12,985
I said don’t call me “babe”!
Come on!

968
00:54:13,276 --> 00:54:16,612
Don’t worry, I’ll buy you a new one
so you’ll have a spare.

969
00:54:17,405 --> 00:54:18,948
Aww...

970
00:54:19,448 --> 00:54:20,825
Really?

971
00:54:21,158 --> 00:54:23,868
You’ll buy Baby Aira a new bag?

972
00:54:23,869 --> 00:54:25,663
You’ll do it for her?
